#!/bin/bash
# Refuse to start a second Watchtower (SPEC.md §spec:container-updates).
#
# §spec:container-updates supports two ways to switch Watchtower on: this systemd
# unit, gated on the operator's configuration, or deploying it from Portainer.
# They are alternatives, not a pair. Two Watchtowers over one Docker engine both
# decide the same container is out of date, and both stop and recreate it - the
# second acting on a container the first has already removed.
#
# The unit's own `docker rm --force kantainer-watchtower` handles a stale copy of
# OURS. This catches the other one: a container the operator deployed from
# Portainer, under a name only they know, from the same image.
#
# Matching on the image rather than the name is what makes that possible. The
# reference is the one the build wrote, so a stack deployed from the image
# Portainer already has - which is the path docs/watchtower.md documents - is
# recognised.

set -oue pipefail

read -r IMAGE_REF < /usr/lib/kantainer/watchtower-image

# --filter is matched by docker against the image reference as given. A stack
# that named a digest or another tag of the same image is not caught here, and
# that is a known gap rather than an oversight: this check exists to catch the
# documented path, not to be a lock.
others="$(docker ps --filter "ancestor=${IMAGE_REF}" --format '{{.Names}}' |
    grep -vx kantainer-watchtower || true)"

if [[ -n "${others}" ]]; then
    cat >&2 <<MSG
Watchtower was not started: one is already running on this machine.

  Already running: ${others//$'\n'/, }
  Image:           ${IMAGE_REF}

Two Watchtowers over one Docker engine race each other: both decide a container
is out of date, both stop and recreate it, and the loser acts on a container
that no longer exists.

Keep ONE of them:

  - to keep the one above, leave this unit alone. Clear
    KANTAINER_WATCHTOWER_ENABLED in your configuration file so it does not start
    on the next machine you flash, and run:

        systemctl disable --now kantainer-watchtower

  - to keep this unit instead, remove the container above - from Portainer, or:

        docker rm --force ${others%%$'\n'*}
        systemctl start kantainer-watchtower
MSG
    exit 1
fi
